{# Appended to the final user turn to keep long conversations on-format.

   Note the tense: `missing_fields` describes the draft as it stood *before*
   this message was read. If the message supplies the rest, the booking is
   complete and the model must summarise rather than keep asking. Without that
   framing the reminder contradicts the system prompt on the turn where the
   user provides everything at once. #}
Reply with the JSON object described in the system message and nothing else.

Remember:
  - Today is {{ now.weekday }}, {{ now.currentDate }} ({{ now.timezone }}).
  - Carry forward every detail already collected.
  - Use null for anything the user has not actually told you.
  - Never ask about duration. It defaults to {{ default_duration }} minutes.
{% if missing_fields %}  - Before reading this message, still unknown: {{ missing_fields | join(", ") }}.
    If this message supplies the rest, do not ask anything further — summarise
    the appointment and ask the user to confirm it.
{% endif -%}
{% if ready_to_confirm %}  - Every required detail is known. Summarise the appointment and ask the user to confirm it.
    If no notes have been collected and you have not already offered, you may
    close that summary by offering to add a note — once, briefly.
{% endif -%}
